U2YRG66)\nIf you prefer, you can pay via Interac at this address: pierrotgilbert@gmail.com\n\nVotre soutien est grandement apprécié ! 😊\nYour support is greatly appreciated!","startDate":"2026-10-13T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Madison Avenue Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"14 Madison Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"[女性限定] Girls’ Night🇨🇦🇯🇵Language Exchange [CAS]🦄🌱","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/events/316362360/","description":"⚠️日本語の案内は下にあります⚠️\n\nWelcome to CAS Japanese x English Girl's Night, where we enjoy small group chats in both languages over tea and the occasional board game 🦄🌱\n\n🌞Perfect for you if...\n☀︎You're looking to make female friends in Toronto.☀︎You've been wanting to try a Meetup event but feel a little nervous.\n\n🎟️Admission: $10\nBring a snack or drink to share and receive 50% off (**only $5**).\nPayment: Cash or e-Transfer only\n(✉️hanano.ishida1@gmail.com)\n\n🎀We'll provide green tea, cups, paper napkins, wet wipes, plates, and board games.\n\n📍Meeting Point: Main Stage on the 1st Floor of the Library\n（If you arrive late, please come to Study Room 1 or 2, or one of the 2nd-floor study rooms.）\n\n🗒️Some House Rules\nIf you can no longer attend, please change your RSVP to \"Not Attending\".\n\nFailure to do so twice may result in removal from the group.\n\n🧸Participation Policy\nThis event is limited to individuals who were assigned female at birth (AFAB).\n\nIf it is at all unclear for us whether you meet this criteria, we reserve the right to remove your RSVP without explanation.\n\nCAS Japanese x English Girl's Nightへようこそ🦄🌱\nおしゃべり、お菓子、お茶、ボードゲームを楽しみながら、日本語と英語の少人数グループで交流する女性限定イベントです♡\n\n🌞こんな方におすすめ\n☀︎トロントで女性の友達を作りたい方\n☀︎Meetupイベントに参加してみたいけれど少し不安がある方\n\n🎟️参加費：10ドル\nお菓子や飲み物をシェア用に持参すると\n参加費が半額の**5ドル**！\n\nお支払い方法：現金またはE-Transferのみ\n(✉️hanano.ishida1@gmail.com)\n\n🎀 緑茶、紙コップ、紙ナプキン、ウェットティッシュ、紙皿、ボードゲームはこちらでご用意しています。\n\n📍集合場所：図書館1階 メインステージ\n（遅れて来られる場合はStudy Room 1 or 2、もしくは2階のスタディルームまで！）\n\n🗒️ご参加にあたってのお願い\n参加できなくなった場合は、必ずRSVPを「Not Attending（欠席）」へ変更してください。\n無断欠席（RSVPを変更しないまま欠席）が2回あった場合は、グループから退会していただく場合があります。\n\n🧸参加条件\nこのイベントは、出生時に女性として割り当てられた方（AFAB：Assigned Female At Birth)を対象としています。\n参加条件を満たしているか判断が難しい場合は、主催者の判断により、事前の説明なくRSVPを取り消す場合があります。","startDate":"2026-10-13T22:50:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Reference Library","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"789 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CAS Meetup Community","url":"https://www.meetup.com/canasian-station/"},"performer":"CAS Meetup Community"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Pickering - Practical Philosophy Meetup 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/events/316685989/","description":"**🏛️ WHAT'S PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY ABOUT?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is a weekly meet-up that brings critical thinkers together for an opportunity to dive deep on a topic, practice communicating, and building a community. All with no ‘official’ philosophy knowledge required! 😎\n\nPractical Philosophy is based on the idea that philosophy should be accessible to all, and not something reserved only for academics. Each week we choose a topic, and the goal is to use the conversation to develop our critical thinking and communication as we explore that topic.\nThe goal is to help develop our Critical Thinking, Communication, and Community 🙌\n\n**📓 HOW DOES IT WORK?**\n\nEach week, we pick one topic and discuss it. The topic for the week is shared, generally in the [Whatsapp group](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP), along with jump-off points to get the conversation going.\n\nWhen groups get bigger than 7-8 people, it’s important that we break into smaller groups. This way we are able to maintain a conversational flow as opposed to having our meetups feel like a discourse or lecture.\n\n**General Meeting Agenda**\nEach Practical Philosophy meet-up follows this general timeline:\n\n* 19:00-19:15 - People arrive and chat, get to know each other before the official start.\n* 19:15-19:25 - Meeting introduction, explanation of Practical Philosophy and the topic for the week, read the guidelines and the overview so attendees know what to expect in terms of timelines.\n* 19:25-20:45 - Break into small groups - introduce yourselves and general thoughts on the topic, open discussion afterwards. At this point the group can review the ‘jump-off’ questions as needed, but they are just there to help guide the conversation. It’s not obligatory to answer them.\n* 20:45-21:00 - Bring everyone back together to discuss conclusions of the topic - each group gives a short 1-minute summary. Organizer concludes the meeting and everyone takes a group photo.\n* 21:00 - The official meeting is over but it’s a great opportunity to get to know people in a non-structured environment, so we often stick around, chat, and get to know each other.\n\n**🧧PRICING?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is operated entirely on voluntary donations! If we are meeting in a café, buy a beverage! Donations are 100% voluntary, but they help us to bring the gift of deep conversation to people around the world. If you'd like to support, you can [donate here](https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/donation-form/donate-to-practical-philosophy)!\n(Practical Philosophy is a registered Canadian charity)\n\n**💛 WHAT PEOPLE SAY ABOUT PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY**\n\n**🗣** “I feel like Philosophy Club helps someone build their own belief system through a series of perspectives while not promoting what’s right and wrong” - Ekam\n\n🗣 “I got hooked from day 1 (the topic was authority) and felt it was the right place for me. I feel it is a place where people can go to learn and discuss new perspectives and increase critical thinking and community by interacting with people who might challenge your point of views but at the same time encourage you to have openness and mind flexibility.” - Daniel\n\n**🤓 FAQ**\n\n* **Do I need to study or read anything to attend?**\n\nNo preparation is necessary. This isn’t a study of other thinkers. We want to know what you think about the topic, not what an old philosopher thought. If you have a perspective from a religion or a school of thought to share, throw it on the table and we’ll discuss it.\n\n* **Is there a specific philosophy that Practical Philosophy is focused on?**\n\nThe goal of our meet-ups is to not have dogmatic discussions, and flex our critical thinking muscles. Because of this, we want to hear from every realm of thought, and don't study a particular school.\n\n* **Is it mostly men that attend?**\n\nSurprisingly, no! Although often, philosophy is seen as a Candelabra affair in a dark room with a bunch of guys, our Practical Philosophy meetups are generally 50/50 between genders, and we don’t meet in any dark rooms.\n\n* **Can I come alone?**\n\nOf course you can, we encourage it :)\n\n* **Can I be late?**\n\nPlease don't be! We do have a 15 minute grace period where we allow people to funnel in while we hang out, but after that if you arrive too late, it disrupts the flow of the conversation.\n\n* **Where do you meet?**\n\nThe location is posted in Meetup and our [Whatsapp](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP) group for this location. It is HIGHLY RECOMMENDED that you join the Whatsapp group! If you want to know what other cities have a Practical Philosophy Club, you can see our chapters on our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/).\n\n🤝**POLICY**\n\nTo respect our members privacy, we ask that no one privately message a member without first getting explicit consent. (This looks like speaking in person and being asked to message privately.) Contacting or texting other participants without prior consent is not permitted and may result in removal from the group. Practical Philosophy reserves the right to enforce this policy at its discretion to maintain a safe and respectful environment.\n\n**PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY CLUB - Philosophy, everywhere. ✨**\n\nWe started in Practical Philosophy back in 2021 and there are now 50+ chapters in 25+ countries, including Canada, Spain, Japan, Mexico and many more! 🗺️\n**\\*\\*\\***\n**Join our [Pickering Whatsapp](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP) 👈**\n**Follow us on [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/practicalphilosophyclub/) 👈**\n**Our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/) 👈**","startDate":"2026-10-13T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Shops at Pickering City Center","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Pickering","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1355 Kingston Road, Pickering, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/"},"performer":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Real Estate Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-real-estate-realist/events/316655357/","description":"Join us for an evening of learning and networking at the Canadian Real Estate Investor Podcast's Toronto Meetup, sponsored by Sherwin-Williams. Whether you are new to real estate investing or looking to enhance your skills, this event is designed for all levels of experience. Our group of seasoned real estate agents, investors, and entrepreneurs will share their knowledge and insights on topics such as mortgages, property management, and investment strategies.\n\nConnect with like-minded individuals in the Toronto real estate community and gain valuable industry connections. Learn from successful investors, benefit from real estate networking opportunities, and discover the keys to successful entrepreneurship in the competitive market. Don't miss out on this event tailored to help you take your real estate investing game to the next level.","startDate":"2026-10-13T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Madison Avenue Pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"14 Madison Avenue, Bloor&Spadina, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Real Estate","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-real-estate-realist/"},"performer":"Toronto Real Estate"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Commerce Toronto | Oct 13, 2026","url":"https://www.meetup.com/techto/events/316553749/","description":"**This is a paid event. You must register and have a ticket to attend.** 👉 **[Commerce Toronto - Oct 13](https://luma.com/commerce-oct-13-2026)**\n\n**Commerce Toronto - where Canada's retail, e-commerce, CPG, and tech communities come together to connect, learn, and grow.**\n\nJoin 200+ founders, operators, and brand builders from the retail, e-commerce, CPG, and tech sectors to unpack the strategies shaping the future of consumer innovation.\n**You'll leave with:**\n\n* Proven strategies to scale your brand, navigate funding, and optimize your launch roadmap\n* Direct access to 200+ vetted industry leaders, founders, and investors building in Canada\n* A look at what's next in consumer innovation through a curated showcase of Canada's top emerging CPG brands\n\n📅 Tuesday\\, Oct 13 \\| 6PM\\- 9PM\n📍 Rotman School of Management\n🎟️ Paid event \\- tickets required \\| Free for TechTO Members\n\n**Register via Luma:** [https://luma.com/commerce-oct-13-2026](https://luma.com/commerce-oct-13-2026)","startDate":"2026-10-13T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"105 St George St","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"105 St George St, Toronto, ON M5S 3E6, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TechTO","url":"https://www.meetup.com/techto/"},"performer":"TechTO"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Council of Solace/Open Meeting","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-rosicrucian-regional-cultural-centre-amorc/events/316677984/","description":"Toronto Lodge invites you to join us for:\n7:00 p.m. Council of Solace\n7:30 p.m. Open Meeting\n**Topic:** “Journey & Destination,” by Johan Arnesson, *Rosicrucian Beacon*, June 2023, Vol. 32, No. 3.\nDestinations can be sweet, the accomplishment pure, and the mountaineering spirit challenged if we understand the purpose of the journey and its value to us. It is a part of the reward for coming this far. We can climb the mountain and peer over the ridge with a sense of satisfaction. We can take time to reflect and determine the course of the next chapter, for the triumph of reaching the destination is but the prelude to another.\nBoth of these events are open to the public.\nMembers are asked to please bring active membership credentials.\nLocation:\n7:00 p.m. Council of Solace - Toronto Lodge, 831 Broadview Avenue, Toronto, ON\n7:30 p.m. Open Meeting - Rosicrucian Cultural Center, 835 Broadview Avenue, Toronto, ON","startDate":"2026-10-13T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Rosicrucians in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-rosicrucian-regional-cultural-centre-amorc/"},"performer":"Rosicrucians in Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free ESL Practice and Support","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-mbglenao/events/316669260/","description":"The Church of St. Timothy is excited to offer support to newcomers in Canada. Our goal is to provide conversational language practice through informal instruction and feedback in a welcoming and diverse community. All levels welcome!\n\nWe invite all new-comers, English language students, visitors to Canada, parents of children temporarily attending schools in Toronto, international university students, and anyone looking to enhance their language skills.\nWe aim to build community where friendships can flourish, in order to help participants establish meaningful connections, learn about life in Toronto, and access practical resources as you settle in to this new city and country.\n\nWe begin every Tuesday at 10:00 a.m. with time to socialize. Our formal program begins at 10:30 a.m.\nEach week we will have different activities and topics, including practicing English conversation, reading short articles, learning about common pronunciation and grammar mistakes, etc.\nOur volunteers would love to get to know you and offer gentle and constructive feedback to help you improve your English!","startDate":"2026-10-13T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"100 Old Orchard Grove","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Old Orchard Grove, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Church of St. Timothy, North Toronto Meetup Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-mbglenao/"},"performer":"Church of St. Timothy, North Toronto Meetup Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantric Family Constellation: Temple of Love & Money","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316686036/","description":"**TANTRIC FAMILY CONSTELLATIONS**\n**Tantric Temple Mysteries**\n\n**This is the project overview only.**\n**Themes and dates may change.**\n\n**To find the exact topic, date and register, please join:**\n\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**About this event**\n\n**Tantric Family Constellations is a group practice combining Archetypal / Family Constellations with a living tantric Temple space.**\n\n**Each meeting has its own theme.**\n\n**For example:**\n\n**Love & Money • Ancient Languages of Love • Love & Loneliness • Masculine & Feminine • Desire & Freedom • Relationship Patterns**\n\n**The theme gives us a field to explore — but every participant discovers their own personal story inside it.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 1 — Discover your pattern**\n\n**We begin by exploring different dimensions of the evening’s theme together.**\n\n**Then each participant goes through a mini-constellation to see their own pattern, model or hidden dynamic.**\n\n**Instead of only thinking about the question, you can see how its different forces are arranged for you:**\n\n**What attracts you?**\n**What do you avoid?**\n**Where does your energy stop?**\n**What are you moving toward?**\n\n**This creates a personal map for the second part of the evening.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 2 — Enter the Temple**\n\n**Then we open the Tantric Temple.**\n\n**The constellation points become living centers in the space.**\n\n**Participants are free to move between them, following their own inner process.**\n\n**You may stay with one energy, move toward another, step away, return, observe what happens in your body, or allow yourself to gradually absorb a quality that previously felt distant.**\n\n**At the same time, you encounter other participants moving through their own paths.**\n\n**Through presence, movement and consensual interaction, the personal constellation becomes a living group field.**\n\n**There is no fixed choreography and no need to perform.**\n\n**You follow your own rhythm.**\n\n**The practice is about allowing yourself to experience, embody and integrate the different energies of the constellation rather than only understand them intellectually.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Why “Temple”?**\n\n**The Temple is a temporary tantric space where symbolic and archetypal energies can be experienced through the body, movement and connection with others.**\n\n**The journey is individual, but it happens inside a shared field.**\n\n**You may discover that a quality which looked abstract during the constellation becomes much more understandable once you can actually move toward it, stay with it and experience it in contact with others.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**No previous constellation or tantra experience is required.**\n\n**Participation is voluntary, and you can always choose your own level of involvement and contact.**\n\n**The space is based on:**\n\n**consent • respect • confidentiality • personal boundaries • freedom of movement**\n\n**This is a transpersonal personal-growth practice.**\n\n**Details, themes, dates and registration:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n\n1. **Regular Ticket — $100 CAD**\n1. **Early Bird Ticket — $65 CAD**\n**If you register and pay before August 31.**\n**3. Supportive Ticket — $55 CAD**\n**For people with limited financial resources.**\n**4. Bring a Friend — $150 CAD for 2 people**\n\n**If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**HOW TO PAY**\n\n**Send an Interac e-Transfer to:**\n**andy.litvinov@gmail.com**\n**After payment, send a screenshot of the confirmation to: t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Please mention which event you are registering for.**\n\n**After registration, you will be added to the participants’ group.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Toronto Tantra community:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-13T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Men's Group Open Circle - Arka Brotherhood","url":"https://www.meetup.com/mens-work-toronto/events/316353519/","description":"**Experience the Arka Brotherhood: A Transformative Community for Growth-Oriented Men**\nLooking to connect with other men on a deeper level? This gathering is a chance to experience *Men’s Work*—a powerful space for growth, reflection, and connection.\nLed by members of the **Arka Brotherhood**, this free 75-minute session offers a glimpse into the kind of work we do in our weekly circles.\n\n**What to Expect:**\n\n* A short intro: “What is Men’s Work?”\n* Core practices and activities from our weekly meetings\n\n**This Is For You If:**\n\n* You’re seeking real connection and community with other men\n* You want to develop leadership, self-discipline, or emotional intelligence\n* You’re ready to confront limiting beliefs and grow\n* You’re curious about Men’s Work but not sure where to begin\n\n***\n\n**Event Details**\n📅 **Date:** Tuesday, Oct. 13, 2026\n🕕 **Time:** Doors open at 6:00 PM, event starts promptly at 6:15 and ends at 7:30 PM\n📍 **Location:** 348 Danforth Ave, Toronto, M4K 1N8\nIn Carrot Commons, Room 212\n🎟️ **Free to attend. RSVP required - space is limited.**\n\n***\n\n**About the Arka Brotherhood**\nArka is a weekly men’s group committed to integrity, accountability, and brotherhood. Our members come from diverse backgrounds and share a commitment to personal growth. We welcome all men - regardless of age, race, faith, or sexual orientation - who are ready to show up honestly and do the work.\n**Learn more about our 14 Point Code and values:** [The Code – ARKA Brotherhood](https://arkabrotherhood.com/the-code/)","startDate":"2026-10-13T22:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Arka @ The Carrot Commons","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"348 Danforth Ave. Room 212, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Men's Work Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/mens-work-toronto/"},"performer":"Men's Work Toronto"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/b/b/4/highres_457835764.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href